<BaseLayout title="Backup, Recovery & Monitoring — Johnaverse" description="Johnathan L.’s approach to backup, recovery, storage, and Grafana monitoring across cloud and local infrastructure." active="cloud">
  <article class="container project-detail"><header class="project-detail-header" data-reveal><a class="back-link" href="/cloud/"><span aria-hidden="true">←</span> Cloud infrastructure</a><p class="eyebrow">RESILIENCE / STORAGE & OBSERVABILITY</p><h1>Recovery is part<br />of the design.</h1><p class="project-lead">I treat backups, recovery planning, and monitoring as connected parts of managing infrastructure. A storage system protects data; an observable system helps explain what happened.</p></header><div class="backup-grid"><section class="project-card" data-reveal><p class="eyebrow">01 / BACKUP</p><h2>Protect the working state.</h2><p>My local environment includes a Synology DS1618+ for storage and backup work. Infrastructure definitions and application data need different handling: one describes how to rebuild a system, while the other preserves the state it depends on.</p></section><section class="project-card" data-reveal><p class="eyebrow">02 / RECOVERY</p><h2>Plan the return to service.</h2><p>My cloud-service work at Hong Kong Telecom included recovery planning and execution. That experience informs how I approach dependencies, restore procedures, and the order in which systems should return.</p></section><section class="project-card" data-reveal><p class="eyebrow">03 / MONITORING</p><h2>Keep the system understandable.</h2><p>I use Grafana for infrastructure monitoring. My Crypto.com work included L1 blockchain infrastructure monitoring, while my Pinax role includes monitoring and optimizing blockchain operations.</p></section></div><div class="prose backup-summary"><h2>Connecting cloud and local infrastructure</h2><p>My current infrastructure work brings together Terraform, container tooling, local storage, and Grafana. The project overviews connect those tools to the systems they support.</p><a class="text-link" href="/cloud/#projects">Explore the infrastructure projects <Icon /></a></div></article>
</BaseLayout>
